        "id": 2052731
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-28T14:48:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I included the device name because it\u0027s required along with the address to pass as parameters to `create_insecure_rfcomm_socket_to_service_record` or any similar method that requires the device. Since the name isn\u0027t available from the grpc request, I had to specify it. \nThis approach was inspired by an instance I found in adapter_client where a test needed a device name that wasn\u0027t provided, so a mock name was used.\nhttps://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/third_party/autotest/files/client/cros/bluetooth/floss/adapter_client.py;l\u003d687?q\u003d%22Test%20device%22\u0026ss\u003dchromiumos%2Fchromiumos%2Fcodesearch:src%2Fthird_party%2Fautotest%2Ffiles%2F",
      "parentUuid": "abc9b976_3d52f3fd",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 391,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 391,
        "endChar": 27
      },
